NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1034,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,2,3,4,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":2.9387,"rank":0.0523,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV001201","role":"target","render":{"description":"Predictions that a sick man will recover, will plough first with a white horse and later with a black horse, and that the black horse will pull the hearse, come true. The horses first harnessed to the hearse refuse, so the black horse has to be harnessed.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43204","original":"Voorloop. \nSchoenmaker vertelt.\n\nOal Kamies noast ons was de haile winter al aon 't sukkeln.\n't Gung dan veur-, dan achteroet,\nBuurman Wessels was 't er op 'n dag hèn west te kieken, hou d' oale 't muik.\n\"Kamies gait achteroet, hai hoal 't nich meer,\" zee hai.\nMoar opa, oal Steffen, zee.\n\"Nee Wessels, Kamies wordt weer beter.\nHai hef nou 'n wit peerd. En 't volgend veurjoar plougt hai 't land mit 'n zwaarde. \nDat zwaarde peerd brengt hum vot.\" \n't Widde wör verkoft en 'n zwaarde kwam d'r veur in de ploats.\nEen buurman hef hiermit de grond pluigd.\nVolgende zömmer störf Kamies.\nVeur de woagen zol 'n peerd van de buren.\nKamies zien aigen har er nog nooit veur west en doarum wol ze hom laiver nich broeken. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV000905","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Before there is a road, the sound of a dog cart and the barking of dogs is heard.","place":"Ter Apel","prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43087","original":"Maar wel is het waar, dat veel mensen in het veen een hondekar hebben horen ratelen. Ook hoorden ze de hond blaffen.\nLang voor er een weg was en voor er later inderdaad een hondekar langs trok.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.87667,7.05972]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV006906","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that one day many soldiers would come with wagons without horses. When the Canadians arrive in 1945, someone remembers this.","place":"Vriescheloo","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43580","original":"Veurloop.\nt Is n hail zet leden. Oabram zee es n moal: “Hier koomt nog ais n haile bult seldoatn. Ik zai ze bie t hoes van H. en bie K en op t haim van Z. Zai hebt woagens bie zuk zunder peerden.\n Toun in 1945 de Canadezen kwamen, was dr nog aine oale, dei zuk dat vertelsel van de spoukkieker in t zin schoot. Hai lag op berre en kun nait best wat zegn, omdat e verlamd was. \nMoar zoveul begreepn wie wel van zien “hoi, hoi”, dat e zegn wol:“Oabram zee t ja al?”","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.06833,7.11389]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV008709","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Noise in the horse stable in the evening is an omen that a horse will kick something to pieces.","place":"Wessinghuizen","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45305","original":"t Gebeurde wol is, dat ze s oavends wat in t peerdstaal heurden. Kiekn deden ze maistied nich, man ze wuzzen wol, dat t peerd gauw wat stukn hou-en zol; door was t n veurbeduudsel van.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.0525,7.075]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Wessinghuizen.","Find Jipsingboertange on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[52.965,7.10139],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Jipsingboertange"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1093,"rank":0.2243,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ046312","role":"member","render":{"description":"Never run in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may pass.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24424","original":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje passeare.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ102104","role":"member","render":{"description":"Some people had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. You should never run in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37102","original":"Yn 'e Harkema en yn Stiensgea ha 'k wol guon kend dy't nachts fan bêd moesten om lykstaesjes to sjen.\nMen moest nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST293","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A road is known as a haunted road. In the evening and at night a white woman can be seen on it, with long, silky hair. Her dress is covered with feathers. Often in the morning some of these little feathers can be seen lying on the road. Her presence seems to have a fatal influence.","place":"Holten","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.J.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13638","original":"Het Witte Wief van de Friezeberg\nDe weg van Rijssen naar Enter is vooral bekend als de spookweg. Vroeger liep langs de eerste helft van die weg door een rij dennen ongeveer 4 meter breed een voetpad dat door de meeste voetgangers gezocht werd om van de schaduw op de anders zoo stoffige zonnige weg te genieten. 's Avonds zou zich daar echter geen sterveling wagen, want dit pad was bij avond en nacht de geliefde wandelplaats van een witte vrouw, door meer dan één gezien. Ze was een slanke vrouw met lang zijachtig haar. Haar wit gewaad was met glanzende veeren bezet en menigmaal kon men 's morgens van die witte veertjes zien liggen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ052415","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator tells of two men who often saw funeral processions. You must never walk in the middle of the road, because an invisible funeral procession can drive you off the road.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25234","original":"Douwe Stavasius fan Grinzer Pein seach lykstaesjes.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane ek. Dy leeft noch.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme, sûnder dat men it sjocht. Dan wurde jo fan 'e wei ôfsmiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Holten belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1047,"rank":0.1423,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ090002","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Hinke Kaert made predictions for two girls. All the predictions later came true.","place":"Dokkum","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33422","original":"Hinke Kaert, dy't letter to Nijebrêge wenne, is ôfkomstich fan Wergea. Se seinen dêr yn Wergea altyd Hinke fan Rutsje. Hja hat twakear troud west. Hja hie fjouwer soannen. De fjirde soan wie in oerwinneling.\nIn frou fan Wergea fortelde my ris: ik haw mei in freondin as greatfanke nei Nijebrêge ta west. Hja sei tsjin my: \"Jo sille noch tsien jier faem bliuwe. Dan sille jo trouwe en fier fuort gean. Jimme sille it goed dwaen en dan weromkomme.\"\nTsjin myn freondinne sei se: \"Jo komme, al ridlik gau, nei oan 'e wei yn in húske to wenjen.\"\nHwat hja dêr foarspeld hat is krekt sa neikom.\nIk bin nei tsien jier troud. Doe binne wy nei Amerika tein. Wy ha dêr bêst buorke. En doe binne wy hjir werkom.\nMyn freondinne krige in healjier letter de tarring. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV012305","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A carter hears his two horses talking, saying they will be sold if he keeps drinking, but he ignores the warning, after which he has to sell his wagon and horses.","place":"Bellingwolde","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43816","original":"Stemmen.\nWas es nmoal n vouerman, dei nog al wat dronk. Bie elke kroeg mos e eevn aan. Hai har twei peern veur de karre. Dei daier wozzen dat ook al wel en begreepn wel, dat et zo nait deur gaon kon; op n duur zol e gain geld meer hebben en den zoln zai vot moutn. \nOp n keer zeg ain van de peern teegn de ander: \"t Zel wel nait laank meer mit ons duurn.\" \nVouerman denkt: \"Hee, kennen n peerd proatn?\" Hai van de woagn of om te lustern wat of ze zegn. Moar as e bie heur komp, zwiegn ze weer en krigt e niks te heurn. \nVan de waarschuwing het hai zuk niks aantrokn en bleef moar zoepm. Net zo laank, tot et mis gung. \nt Geld roakde op; de woagn mos vot en de peern dr bie.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ017911","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Two people step aside for a funeral procession; a short time later someone actually dies.","place":"Sumar","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20224","original":"Ik en Wibe Weening hienen op in joun yn 'e Harkema oan 't kuijerjen west. Doe sei Wibe tsjin my: \"Mast even út 'e wei gean.\" Wy stienen in skoftsje oan 'e kant fan 'e wei. \"Nou kinne wy wol wer op 'e wei\", sei er. Hy hie in lykstaesje foarbygean sjoen. Mar ik seach neat. 't Wie Pytsje Alma har man, dêr't er de bigraffenis fan sjoen hie. Dy is koart dêrnei stoarn.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","2 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":2},"on_success":{"chime":2,"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6258,"rank":0.0,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL000404","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Seeing a witte juffer (white lady); playing at being a witte juffer with a white sheet around oneself.","place":"Ingen","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209537","original":"Witte vrouwen . Bij de pas (aanplant van wilgen of populieren met onderhout van elzen en essen) (lag dicht bij de woning van de zegslieden) zag men soms een witte gedaante lopen. Maar sommigen geloofden niet aan de witte juffer, zo werd Han Briene er van verdacht, dat hij soms de kinderen bang wilde maken door voor witte juffer te spelen (hij deed zich dan een laken om) Enige jongens wilden met Jas Gaosbeek, een niet volwaardige zoon van een bakker, een grap uithalen. Zij sloegen zich lakens om en gingen wandelen op een plaats, waar Jas passeren moest. Deze ging er echter niet voor door, maar begon de \"juffer\", die hij het eerst te pakken kreeg af te ranselen. De andere jongens sloegen toen op de vlucht","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL002208","role":"variant","render":{"description":"In the evening, mistaking a stick with a newspaper on it for a witte juffer (white lady).","place":"Ochten","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210065","original":"Er moet een witte juffer gelopen hebben op het Zand (fruitteeltbedrijf) bij het witte hek (dit stond op de weg, die tussen twee kolken doorloopt. Keuken, hij was toen 18 jaar, ging eens met een kameraad naar Eldik (buurtschap) om een vriend te bezoeken. Deze bleek niet thuis. Op de dijk op de plaats waar beneden het witte hek stond, was een stok met krant er om gezet, als teken voor de castreur dat er \"keujes\" moesten gesneden worden. Janus stapte tegen deze stok aan, deze ging heen en weer, de kameraad beweerde, dat hij een witte juffer had gezien en was van dit idee, ook de volgende dag, niet af te brengen","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"HOL002604","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A white maiden who asks the way throws a hat full of money and disappears.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210163","original":"Berend, den dakuil (een Van Uden) smeerde de daken van binnen aan met kalk, vandaar dat hij deze bijnaam kreeg. Eens liep Berend op de Grotebrugse grintweg bij de Twaalf Apostelen (straatje) toen een witte juffer hem de weg vroeg naar het veer. Berend zei haar die en nadat hij dit gedaan had, gooide zij hem de hoed vol met \"Berliner daolder\". Driemaal was Berend dit overkomen. Bij het veer gekomen wilde Berend haar bedanken, maar hij kreeg geen kans daartoe: zij was verdwenen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Gelderland an object was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1962.","That card names an object. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"5c5dc9311c1caea4","accepted_hashes":["1d77186fb871e34f7e79b5e2fd44349e93c2c3da8b976f253452fdf8c96553ca","2229204b90818e7259feab6a32e5c572d6b957586e3c059bbe400a3bc57a3fd5","7acb1ae0c7bae7b635ff2194288db156b89e54fb172fa3ccf87a532f64d2de3f","db13fd21d544b5f70b517a934021991d5f477a6399bb2aec243715323482599f","fa9e6c0831add33ceb1322312a9608eed9c29577f20f7e43ab4e1575d2a8dddf","fb940db49d9d125cec2907bb7ec29b8c3cbcd18d3ab5c475bc74ab6b700875e4"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0957,"rank":0.4994,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL001815","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Werewolves wear a skin and make themselves carried; a place where they can be heard.","place":"Lienden","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209954","original":"Weerwolven hadden een vel om. Ze hadden er plezier om bij iemand op de kruiwagen, ook op de rug te springen. Die dit overkwam moest de weerwolf kruien of dragen. En die was zwaar, hoor!\nJuffrouw Van Kalkeren weet nog, hoe haar vader (geb. 1861) altijd blij was geweest, dat hij \"de krump”\"(= de kromming, bocht) van de Groene Straat, waarin hij voor zijn huwelijk woonde, was gepasseerd. In die \"krump\" zaten altijd weerwolven te brommen. (Ik ben na afloop van deze opname door de Groene Straat teruggegaan, terwijl het al donker was en heb geen gebrom gehoord).","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ063812","role":"member","render":{"description":"In Parken and in Rottefalle witte wijven (white women) haunt.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27145","original":"Hjir yn 'e Parken spoeken wite wiven en dat wie ek yn 'e Rottefalle it gefal.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ057303","role":"member","render":{"description":"Several people have seen two witte wijven (white women) in the woods.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25852","original":"Witte wiven gingen altyd door 't bos van Jild Dyk. En so ferdwenen se weer. 't Waren twee witte frouljuu.\nDit gebeurde faak. Forskeidene hebben se sien.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ061710","role":"member","render":{"description":"On the heath in Drenthe witte wijven (white women) haunt.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/26899","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Lienden belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0353,"rank":0.4407,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"ZEEUW051","role":"card","render":{"description":"In Grauw it sometimes happened, if you went out late in the evening, that the Witte Juffer (White Lady) kept you company.","place":"Graauw","prov":"Zl.","year":1921,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"L.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38977","original":"Witte Juffers\n\nOp Grauw gebeurde het soms, als ge 's avonds laat op pad ging, dat ge gezelschap kreegt van de Witte Juffer.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"TINNEV038","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man makes a bet that he dares to ask the wit wief (white woman) from the woods to dance. They dance until the man can go on no longer and drops dead.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22384","original":"25. DE WITTE WIEF VAN MONTFELAND\nIen de bös rond Montfeland zitte witte wief die gin mins kwaod doen, ai eur teminste met rös laot. \nIemand uut Beak, dén met 'n zatte kop aan zon wief vroeg of ze met um wol danse, kosse die vroag 't lève. Zi'j bleef de hele nach met um aan 't deurdanse. De man wol iedere kier opholle, mao dat \nging niet. Hi'j mos deurdrèje, ook toe te nie meer kon. 't Zweit liep um nèven 't lief as offe ien de bare zon aan 't rogmèje was. Hi'j smeken um toch op te holle, mor 't wief ging deur. Endelijk, ien de margetied, viel de man dood veur eur vuut neer. …","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE070d","role":"card","render":{"description":"The narrator is heading home with a few friends. On the way they meet a white girl moving quickly. She floats towards a cottage. They go to investigate. Later an old man hanged himself, and people say it was connected with this. The minister is very sceptical about the story.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12149","original":"Wite juffers\nWat ik hjir yn 'e Westerein sels sjoen ha. Dat is no lyn, ik tink sa'n fiif-, seis-, sânenfyftich jier. Myn kammeraat en ik gyngen de jûntiid om in oere of alve stadichoan nei hûs ta. Doe troffen wy in pear jongelju en dy hâlden ús oan. De man sei: 'Sjoch, wat is dêr? Dêr is in famke midden yn 'e sûkerei. By it hûs dêre is it allegearre út en tsjuster, mar hoe kin dan sa'n wyt famke der yn 't lân weze?' Doe seach ik it ek. Ik sei: 'Dan moatte wy dêr ris even sjen'. Mar dat famke avensrarde tige hurd en wy koenen sjen, dat it net gie, mar dat it sweefde. It hie de grutte sawat fan in gewoan famke, en sniewyt. Ik sei: 'No, sille wy ris sjen? …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_08A_001","role":"card","render":{"description":"Dwelling place of witte wieven (white women); they are helpful, and if left alone they do nothing.","place":"Mander","prov":"Ov.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128452","original":"Bels: Doar hebt ze ok wat vuindn, nich, doe ze doar vrower an 't bouwn warn west, nich, en an 't eand har der dan nen kôm koffie of melk, dee har der kloar stoan zoa vertöln ze van oolds oet, nich.\nIk: Woar hebt dee witte wiew dan eigenlik in lewd dan?\nB: Dee hebt in de holn lewd.\nIk: Was dat een of andre beult, woar at ze inzatn?\nB: Joa ze zatn in ne beult, dat warn twee beultn, dee hebt ze later nog ôpgrövn, dokter Hijszeler is der wa met an 't grewn west met dee beultn, nich? …","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ018012","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Three white ladies, sisters, always haunt a haunted spot. Later that place was also said to be called the 'Susterwei'.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20251","stain":"three"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"WEV014306","role":"card","render":{"description":"Nobody dares to buy a house in which witte juffers (white ladies) walk.","place":"Meerland","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44759","original":"Bie Appingedam ston eerder n hoes, woor t in spookde.\nZai zaggen er widde juffers in loopn.\nEt is n poar keer te koop aanboden, moar gainaine dus t koopn. \nHou of t er loater mit goan is, wait ik nait.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Garyp. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c5","object":"window","text":"Garyp"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c5","word":"three","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P1","difficulty":1.1309,"rank":0.9121,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"EDJSL003","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand tells his girl that he has an errand to run, and that if she meets a vicious dog she must give it her handkerchief. She does indeed meet a dog, throws the handkerchief at it and flees. During the meal it is seen that he has pieces of a handkerchief between his teeth. When his room is searched, the belt that turns someone into a werewolf is found. As soon as the belt is thrown into the fire, the farmhand, who was working far away, is standing by the oven trying to jump into the fire. After the belt has burned, the farmhand is released.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1894,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9505","original":"De weerwolf\nEr was eens een boerenknecht die soms een weerwolf was.\nDe knecht vrijde met een van de meiden, maar zij wist van de prins geen kwaad. Op een keer waren ze een eind buiten het dorp gaan wandelen. Toen ze op huis aangingen, viel de schemer in.\nOpeens had de knecht zin weerwolf te worden.\nHij zei tegen de meid: \"Ik moet hier even een boodschap doen. Loop jij maar vast door, ik haal je wel in. Mocht je een kwade hond tegenkomen, die je wil bijten, gooi hem dan mijn zakdoek toe. Dan heeft hij iets om zijn tanden in te zetten, terwijl jij ervandoor gaat.\"\nHij ging weg, en een poosje later zag ze een grote hond op zich afkomen. Ze gooide hem de zakdoek toe en zette het op een lopen. Het dier scheurde de zakdoek aan flarden en at hem op. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BOEKV179","role":"card","render":{"description":"A youth is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the youth's teeth. Werewolves always wear a band around their waist. The farmer the youth works for burns the band. The werewolf still tries to get into the fire, but he is held back. When the band has burned, the youth is an ordinary person again.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1896,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"G.J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35060","original":"Van een Weerwolf.\n\nOp de Achterste hoef woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op een eigenaardige manier zijn ze daar achter gekomen.\nDie knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buiten dorps (1) geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet meer zoo heel ver van huis toen voelde hij een onweerstaanbare lust om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte het natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens (2) van den weg af bij genen boer zijn; ga gij maar door: ik zal u wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die op u aan bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij misschien wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"SINBRABSAG185","role":"card","render":{"description":"A young man is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the young man's teeth. This is how they know he is a werewolf.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46940","original":"No. 185. Op de Achterste hoef bij Bladel woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op 'n vreemde manier zijn ze dat aan de weet gekomen. Die knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buitendorps geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker, toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet ver meer van huis toen hij een onweerstaanbaren lust voelde om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte dat natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens van den weg af bij genen boer zijn, ga gij maar door: ik zal oe wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die naar oe bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST009","role":"card","render":{"description":"A couple go for a walk in the evening. The boy has to relieve himself, but before he disappears into the bushes he advises the girl that if a beast attacks her, she should throw her handkerchief in front of its mouth. A dangerous beast does indeed come at the girl. She throws her handkerchief in front of its jaws and the beast tears it apart. When the boy comes back, the girl sees that he has remnants of her handkerchief between his teeth. She now knows he is a werewolf and tells him so. The boy disappears and never came back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13223","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen vrijer bracht 's avonds z'n meisje naar huis. Onderweg zei ie: \"Ik moet even mijn behoefte doen. Als je in tussentijd een dier of zoiets op je af ziet komen, gooi het dan je zakdoek voor z'n kop.\" Toen de jongen weg was, kwam er een dier op het meisje aangelopen. Ze slingerde haar zakdoek voor z'n muil en het beest verscheurde hem. Even later kwam de jongen terug en hij vroeg zijn meisje of er iets gebeurd was. Ze vertelde wat er was voorgevalllen en terwijl keek ze hem strak aan. Toen zei ze hem: \"Ik geloof, dat jij het beest bent geweest, want je hebt de stukken zakdoek nog tussen je tanden zitten\" Onmiddellijk was de vrijer verdwenen, en het meisje heeft hem nooit teruggezien.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with H. 12 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"5c5dc9311c1caea4","accepted_hashes":["290f06d0b4bdac07c8fe22f8682460921fe00905a544621a2ef60d52478518fb","af42c84abe79c75f53da75e157e6faefb69fb222a4efe43fa4d959ef1f46691e","e1c55bafbd804bd3ec16d8c12282c9c146374c2c5c34d0855d530a1f3d8ced15","e736da379d4fa56c31b968f16236666464478c4c0d1cede1af7ffcf73fb8109f"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1909,"rank":0.6738,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL002419","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Appearance and doings of werewolves.","place":"Opheusden","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210126","original":"Dirk Winsen vertelde: \"Hij ister vannach weer gewes\" Hij was een weerwolf. Weerwolven liepen \"op-te-vier\" nl. op handen en voeten. Men kon dit aan hun vingers zien, want ze hadden \"zwil (= eelt) opte kneukels\" (= gewrichten). Ze hadden een \"vel\" om, dat ze ergens vandaan haalden. Waarvandaan wist R. niet. Ze lieten een brommend geluid horen en hadden vurige ogen. Om twaalf uur moesten ze er op uit om te gaan \"wèrwolve\". Hun lichaam mocht dan nog wel op het bed liggen, maar de geest was er uit, die was bezig het de mensen lastig te maken, Ze liepen de late wandelaars voor de voeten, gooiden mensen met kar en paard van de dijk, maar wat een geluk was: er bleek na deze behandeling niets gebroken. Plotseling kwamen de weerwolven tegen de dijk op. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ115519","role":"member","render":{"description":"A werewolf is someone who is never full: he just keeps on eating. One of seven boys in a household is a werewolf.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1977,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/31124","original":"In wjerwolf is ien dy't net sêd kin. 't Kin neat skele hoefolle er hawn hat, hy kin altyd wol wèr ite. Ien út in húshâlding fan sawn jonges is in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ046513","role":"member","render":{"description":"Of seven boys born in succession, one is a werewolf or a devil-banisher.","place":"Boelenslaan","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24459","original":"Fan ien fan 'e sawn jonges, dêr't net in fanke tusken is, is ien in wearwolf of in duvelbanner.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ054504","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven boys born in succession is a werewolf. The narrator tells of a boy, one of seven sons, who is a werewolf and feels the urge to tear all sorts of things apart.","place":"Boelenslaan","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25484","original":"Ien fan sawn opelkoarfolgjende jonges is in wjerwolf.\nYn 'e Moedershoeke, hjir yn 'e Boelensloane wenne Brant Veenstra. Dy hie sawn jonges. Ien fan dy jonges is Hindrik. Dat wie in wjerwolf. Syn eigen heit sei: \"Hindrik is in raren, 't is in forskuorreling.\"\nOp in kear siet er op 't hûske. Syn broer Germ pleage him oan 'e bûtenkant. Doe fleach Hindrik sa fan 't hûske ôf mei de broeken by 't gat del op syn broer ta en seamde him ôf.\nHy ropte soms mei de tosken de bûsdoeken útelkoar.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Opheusden belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.065,"rank":0.5897,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL001024","role":"card","render":{"description":"People who do not touch werewolves; a man who is out as a werewolf is in two places at once; werewolves wear a skin.","place":"Opheusden","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209732","original":"Gaart en Stoffel van Brenk konden weerwolven. Als deze en ook andere personen daarmee bezig waren, moest men ze niet “omlegge” op het bed, want dan ging het mis met hen. Mensen zagen \"Stomp\" onder de noteboom liggen, maar ook lag hij thuis op bed. Hij was toen aan het weerwolven. Weerwolven hadden een vel om.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ058210","role":"door","render":{"description":"A werewolf is one of seven successive sons.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25993","original":"In wjerwolf is ien fan sawn opelkoar folgjende jonges, wurdt der altyd sein.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST189","role":"card","render":{"description":"Three people tell that late one evening they met a big dog with fiery eyes that jumped on their backs. Only at the edge of the field did it jump off and vanish. The dog vanished near a farm already known as uncanny, because the farmhand there said that the cows several times jumped up at the stroke of midnight while the stable doors flew open by themselves.","place":"Puiflijk","prov":"Gld.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.v.d.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13453","original":"Spookdieren\nMij is eens door drie verschillende personen op zeer verschillende tijden meegedeeld dat op de Waaldijk tussen Boven-Leeuwen en Druten 's avonds in pikdonker plotseling een abnormale grote hond, die plotseling verscheen, hen zwijgend met vurige ogen volgde en even plots aan de grens van Druten verdween. Beide personen waren niet bijgelovig maar hadden van angst 't zweet op de rug staan van angst, temeer daar de hond verdween bij een boerderij waar 't niet \"pluis\" scheen te zijn. Een knecht op deze boerderij vertelde mij eens hoe verscheidene malen 's nachts de koeien om klokslag 12 uur opsprongen en staldeuren openvlogen zonder 'n aanwijsbare oorzaak. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c2","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c3","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.8074,"rank":0.9425,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ021204","role":"top","render":{"description":"A minister's dead wife kept coming back and standing by the fire of the hearth pit.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20724","half":"top"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV004601","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Especially people who lived wicked lives, suicides and murdered people are seen again after their death.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ115019","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The devil banishers catch the ghost in a large chest and tie the donkey behind a horse-drawn wagon. Both horses pulling the devil banishers' wagon bolt and run straight into the canal. The ghost and one of the devil banishers drown.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CBOEK084","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"She flees the convent where she is living at the time and comes back to haunt the rooms of her ancestors' house. She wears a white nun's habit that is easy to see at night. Because she wears a dark hood, her head is not noticed. That is why people think a headless woman wanders the ruins.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ013416","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The man wanted to chase her away, but when she stood up she was suddenly a very big woman. She picked the man up and threw him in the ditch. After he had climbed out of the water, she walked beside him for quite a while. Until she suddenly just sank away into the ground.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"KEMP181","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The body parts come together and form an old man. It is a ghost that keeps giving the soldier orders: that he must go to the cellar and lift a stone, and so on. The man boldly refuses and makes the ghost do everything itself. Three pots of gold turn out to be hidden in the farmstead. The spirit tells the soldier to give one pot to the church and one to the poor, and he may keep one himself, as thanks for releasing the ghost, who had been wicked in his life and exploited the poor.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"KEMP151","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The next day they heard others say that the Sint-Jansbos was haunted, and that the count of Schaloen was driven around there at night because he had not fulfilled his obligations when he took possession of the wood.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"CJ108604","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He strikes a temple and his brother dies. The farmhouse is demolished, but later a white woman haunts the place.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"CJ021204","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"She wanted the money hidden in the hearth pit to be divided among the orphans and widows. The minister handed her a white handkerchief as a sign that it would be done. The handkerchief burned in his hand. After that she never came back.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"CBOEK457","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"I was told that one evening, although it was dead calm outside, an infernal racket broke out in that barn. Wagon planks were thrown about. Finally the doors flew wide open; it was a terrible noise, but nothing could be seen. Several times an animal, which looked like a dog, was also seen there; it would walk a stretch alongside passers-by and then vanish as mysteriously as it had come.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0456"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"VODA_035_15","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"From then on the farmhand hears the noise of the winnowing mill every night. When he goes to look the noise stops, but when he wants to sleep it starts again. In the end the farmhand cannot stand it any longer and has to give notice.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"GENDT006","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Before she can go on pilgrimage, however, she falls ill and dies. Her husband finds the money, does not know what it was for, and spends it. His wife appears to him and asks him to fulfil her promise to the neighbour after all, and even to double it. As a pledge he must throw a handkerchief to her, and she throws it back with her handprint on it. An alms of wheat must also be doubled.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ079605","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"She then killed herself, and that is why the gate never closes anymore.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0435"},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘minister’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c9"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c9"],"stack":["c1","c9"]},"found_card":{"card":"c9"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.4105,"rank":1.1193,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ099215","role":"member","render":{"description":"Ever since a man was murdered on the Godloas singel, it has been haunted there.","place":"Mûnein","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36619","original":"Op 'e Godloas singel spûket it. Dêr is ris in man formoarde. Sûnt spûket er dêr.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ099402","role":"member","render":{"description":"The Stobbehoek is also called Teadehoekje because a man named Teade was murdered there long ago. People did not dare to pass by there because it was haunted.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36647","original":"Op Stobbehoek, ek wol Teadehoekje neamd, tusken Drachten en Boarnburgum, is froeger in man formoarde woarn, in sekere Teade. Dêr is de namme Teadehoekje fan. De minsken doarsten dêr froeger net lâns omdat it dêr spoeke.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ099313","role":"member","render":{"description":"Someone was murdered on the Godloassingel [godless men's lane]. It is still haunted there.","place":"Mûnein","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36643","original":"Op 'e Godloassingel, dêr is ien formoarde woarn. Dy spûket dêr nòch.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"EGGEN002303","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Belief that a Freemason was murdered by the devil.","place":"Sibbe","prov":"L.","year":1970,"code":null,"initials":"C.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/207917","original":"Ook verdient vermelding zijn mededeling over iemand uit Heerlen, die, lid van de vrijmetselaars, begin deze eeuw gewurgd werd door de duivel. Tenminste, dat was de algemene conclusie, die echter gebaseerd was op 't feit, dat de hals van de vermoorde duidelijk de indrukken van langnagelige klauwen te zien gaf.","lang":"Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Sibbe belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.2143,"rank":0.7917,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer lives in a haunted farmhouse. When an old soldier comes begging, the farmer asks whether he will keep watch.","place":"Uitdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1903,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35028","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEMP173","role":"half","render":{"description":"Fortunately he knows that you must be bold with ghosts and never give them their way. He follows the ghost but refuses to carry out the tasks it gives him. The next day the craftsman has grey hair, but he is in possession of a treasure. From then on he can live off his wealth.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ015407","role":"half","render":{"description":"When she later goes to feed the pigs, the child's ghost keeps appearing. The child keeps putting its little hands on the pig trough.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ073804","role":"half","render":{"description":"Then Ruerd threatened to knock him down if he did not wait. The other then stopped. When Ruerd reached him, the other grabbed him several times and threw him over the trees. The next day they found him unconscious with all his ribs broken.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"At midnight the soldier sees six ghosts pass by; high-ranking officers who dig a hole by the haystack with their sabres. The ghosts pull up a kettle of gold coins and hide it again. In the morning the soldier asks the farmhand to help him dig. By the haystack they find the kettle of gold and take it. At night the ghosts come to dig again, but find nothing and never return. The farmer is pleased and offers the soldier lodging and a reward. The soldier accepts the lodging, but by now he has enough money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"six"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ093904","role":"half","render":{"description":"He died in an accident with a horse and now his treasure lies there under the ground. The old man haunts the place and people are terrified. The old man keeps coming closer.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ082909","role":"half","render":{"description":"The man cannot bear it and fetches the minister. The minister says to the ghost: 'If you are of God, come to me; if you are of the devil, depart.' The ghost disappears and never comes back.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘farmer’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c5","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c5"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1","word":"six","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
